      a: "Under Sec 25, an agreement made without consideration is generally void. Exceptions include promises made out of natural love and affection between close relatives, promises to compensate someone for a voluntary past act, written promises to pay a time-barred debt, actual completed gifts, and creation of an agency, plus certain charitable subscriptions - but a promise conditioned on an unlawful act still isn't enforceable.",
